# Decided
- The issue's suggested fix as given: R defaults to std::string for
  json_extract and json_quote, in both the legacy (C++17) wrappers and the
  C++20 wrappers of dev/builtin/functions/json.h.
- json_quote keeps its R rather than being fixed to std::string, so
  json_quote<float> (tests/json.cpp) and every explicit R still compile.
- Tests written first: json_extract gets a SECTION, json_quote a plain block
  (its other cases are plain blocks; a lone SECTION would rerun them).
  Each pins the result type with STATIC_REQUIRE and the value.

